Provenance
----------

icloud-for-linux is an independent implementation.  It was written from scratch
in Rust for this repository.  No source code from any other project is vendored,
copied or transliterated here.

The goal it pursues - a local-first iCloud Drive filesystem for Linux - comes
from the community project:

    icloud-linux - https://github.com/IsmaeelAkram/icloud-linux
    Author: Ismaeel Akram

That project is credited for the idea and for demonstrating that the idea is
worth building.  It ships no LICENSE file, which means it is "All rights
reserved" by default; nothing from it is reused in this repository, and its
code must not be copied into it.  If you want the two projects to share code,
obtain an explicit license grant from the upstream author first.

The design decisions in this repository are documented independently in
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and are our own.

